"applications)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:192
msgid "`Key#createVerify([hashAlgorithm])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:194
msgid ""
"Creates a `crypto.Verifier` specialized to use this Key (and the correct "
"public key algorithm to match it). The returned Verifier has the same API"
" as a regular one, except that the `verify()` function takes only the "
"target signature as an argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:201 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:322
msgid ""
"`hashAlgorithm` -- optional String name of hash algorithm to use, any"
"                    supported by OpenSSL are valid, usually including"
"                    `sha1`, `sha256`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:205
msgid "`v.verify(signature[, format])` Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:207
msgid "`signature` -- either a Signature object, or a Buffer or String"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:208
msgid ""
"`format` -- optional String, name of format to interpret given String "
"with.             Not valid if `signature` is a Signature or Buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:211
msgid "`Key#createDiffieHellman()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:212
msgid "`Key#createDH()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:214
msgid ""
"Creates a Diffie-Hellman key exchange object initialized with this key "
"and all necessary parameters. This has the same API as a "
"`crypto.DiffieHellman` instance, except that functions take `Key` and "
"`PrivateKey` objects as arguments, and return them where indicated for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:219
msgid ""
"This is only valid for keys belonging to a cryptosystem that supports DHE"
" or a close analogue (i.e. `dsa`, `ecdsa` and `curve25519` keys). An "
"attempt to call this function on other keys will yield an `Error`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:223
msgid "Private keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:225
msgid "`parsePrivateKey(data[, format = 'auto'[, options]])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:227
msgid ""
"Parses a private key from a given data format and returns a new "
"`PrivateKey` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:236
msgid ""
"`ssh`, `openssh`: new post-OpenSSH 6.5 internal format, produced by"
"                   `ssh-keygen -o`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:240
msgid "`dnssec`: `.private` format output by `dnssec-keygen` etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:242
msgid ""
"`filename` -- Optional String, name for the key being parsed"
"               (eg. the filename that was opened). Used to generate"
"               Error messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:248
msgid "`generatePrivateKey(type[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:250
msgid "Generates a new private key of a certain key type, from random data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:254
msgid ""
"`type` -- String, type of key to generate. Currently supported are "
"`'ecdsa'`           and `'ed25519'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:256 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:463
#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:480
msgid "`options` -- optional Object, with keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:257
msgid ""
"`curve` -- optional String, for `'ecdsa'` keys, specifies the curve to "
"use.            If ECDSA is specified and this option is not given, "
"defaults to            using `'nistp256'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:261
msgid "`PrivateKey.isPrivateKey(obj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:263
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the given object is a valid `PrivateKey` object created"
" by a version of `sshpk` compatible with this one."
msgstr ""

