msgid "`PrivateKey#type`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:274
msgid "`PrivateKey#size`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:279
msgid "`PrivateKey#curve`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:285
msgid "`PrivateKey#toBuffer([format = 'pkcs1'])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:292
msgid ""
"`format` -- String name of format to use, valid options are listed under"
"              `parsePrivateKey`. Note that ED25519 keys default to "
"`openssh`             format instead (as they have no `pkcs1` "
"representation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:296
msgid "`PrivateKey#toString([format = 'pkcs1'])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:300
msgid "`PrivateKey#toPublic()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:302
msgid ""
"Extract just the public part of this private key, and return it as a "
"`Key` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:305
msgid "`PrivateKey#fingerprint([algorithm = 'sha256'])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:307
msgid "Same as `this.toPublic().fingerprint()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:309
msgid "`PrivateKey#createVerify([hashAlgorithm])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:311
msgid "Same as `this.toPublic().createVerify()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:313
msgid "`PrivateKey#createSign([hashAlgorithm])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:315
msgid ""
"Creates a `crypto.Sign` specialized to use this PrivateKey (and the "
"correct key algorithm to match it). The returned Signer has the same API "
"as a regular one, except that the `sign()` function takes no arguments, "
"and returns a `Signature` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:326
msgid "`v.sign()` Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:328
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:330
msgid "`PrivateKey#derive(newType)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:332
msgid ""
"Derives a related key of type `newType` from this key. Currently this is "
"only supported to change between `ed25519` and `curve25519` keys which "
"are stored with the same private key (but usually distinct public keys in"
" order to avoid degenerate keys that lead to a weak Diffie-Hellman "
"exchange)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:339
msgid ""
"`newType` -- String, type of key to derive, either `ed25519` or "
"`curve25519`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:341
msgid "Fingerprints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:343
msgid "`parseFingerprint(fingerprint[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:345
msgid ""
"Pre-parses a fingerprint, creating a `Fingerprint` object that can be "
"used to quickly locate a key by using the `Fingerprint#matches` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:350
msgid "`fingerprint` -- String, the fingerprint value, in any supported format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:351
msgid "`options` -- Optional Object, with properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:352
msgid ""
"`algorithms` -- Array of strings, names of hash algorithms to limit"
"             support to. If `fingerprint` uses a hash algorithm not on"
"             this list, throws `InvalidAlgorithmError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:355
msgid ""
"`hashType` -- String, the type of hash the fingerprint uses, either `ssh`"
"               or `spki` (normally auto-detected based on the format, but"
"               can be overridden)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:358
msgid ""
"`type` -- String, the entity this fingerprint identifies, either `key` or"
"           `certificate`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:361
msgid "`Fingerprint.isFingerprint(obj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:363
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the given object is a valid `Fingerprint` object "
"created by a version of `sshpk` compatible with this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:370
msgid "`Fingerprint#toString([format])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:372
msgid "Returns a fingerprint as a string, in the given format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:376
msgid ""
"`format` -- Optional String, format to use, valid options are `hex` and"
"             `base64`. If this `Fingerprint` uses the `md5` algorithm, "
"the             default format is `hex`. Otherwise, the default is "
"`base64`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:380
msgid "`Fingerprint#matches(keyOrCertificate)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:382
msgid ""
"Verifies whether or not this `Fingerprint` matches a given `Key` or "
"`Certificate`. This function uses double-hashing to avoid leaking timing "
"information. Returns a boolean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:386
msgid ""
"Note that a `Key`-type Fingerprint will always return `false` if asked to"
" match a `Certificate` and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:391
msgid ""
"`keyOrCertificate` -- a `Key` object or `Certificate` object, the entity "
"to                       match this fingerprint against"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:394
msgid "Signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:396
msgid "`parseSignature(signature, algorithm, format)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:398
msgid ""
"Parses a signature in a given format, creating a `Signature` object. "
"Useful for converting between the SSH and ASN.1 (PKCS/OpenSSL) signature "
"formats, and also returned as output from "
"`PrivateKey#createSign().sign()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:402
msgid ""
"A Signature object can also be passed to a verifier produced by "
"`Key#createVerify()` and it will automatically be converted internally "
"into the correct format for verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:408
msgid ""
"`signature` -- a Buffer (binary) or String (base64), data of the actual"
"                signature in the given format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:410
msgid ""
"`algorithm` -- a String, name of the algorithm to be used, possible "
"values                are `rsa`, `dsa`, `ecdsa`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:412 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:429
msgid "`format` -- a String, either `asn1` or `ssh`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:414
msgid "`Signature.isSignature(obj)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:416
msgid ""
"Returns `true` if the given object is a valid `Signature` object created "
"by a version of `sshpk` compatible with this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:423
msgid "`Signature#toBuffer([format = 'asn1'])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:425
msgid "Converts a Signature to the given format and returns it as a Buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:431
msgid "`Signature#toString([format = 'asn1'])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:433
msgid "Same as `this.toBuffer(format).toString('base64')`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:435
msgid "Certificates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:437
msgid ""
"`sshpk` includes basic support for parsing certificates in X.509 (PEM) "
"format and the OpenSSH certificate format. This feature is intended to be"
" used mainly to access basic metadata about certificates, extract public "
"keys from them, and also to generate simple self-signed certificates from"
" an existing key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:442
msgid ""
"Notably, there is no implementation of CA chain-of-trust verification, "
"and only very minimal support for key usage restrictions. Please do the "
"security world a favour, and DO NOT use this code for certificate "
"verification in the traditional X.509 CA chain style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:447
msgid "`parseCertificate(data, format)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:451
msgid "`data` -- a Buffer or String"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:452
msgid ""
"`format` -- a String, format to use, one of `'openssh'`, `'pem'` (X.509 "
"in a             PEM wrapper), or `'x509'` (raw DER encoded)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:455
msgid "`createSelfSignedCertificate(subject, privateKey[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:459 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:476
msgid "`subject` -- an Identity, the subject of the certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:460
msgid ""
"`privateKey` -- a PrivateKey, the key of the subject: will be used both "
"to be                 placed in the certificate and also to sign it "
"(since this is                 a self-signed certificate)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:464 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:481
msgid ""
"`lifetime` -- optional Number, lifetime of the certificate from now in"
"               seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:466 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:483
msgid ""
"`validFrom`, `validUntil` -- optional Dates, beginning and end of"
"                              certificate validity period. If given"
"                              `lifetime` will be ignored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:469 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:486
msgid "`serial` -- optional Buffer, the serial number of the certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:470 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:487
msgid "`purposes` -- optional Array of String, X.509 key usage restrictions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:472
msgid "`createCertificate(subject, key, issuer, issuerKey[, options])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:477
msgid "`key` -- a Key, the public key of the subject"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:478
msgid "`issuer` -- an Identity, the issuer of the certificate who will sign it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:479
msgid "`issuerKey` -- a PrivateKey, the issuer's private key for signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:489
msgid "`Certificate#subjects`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:491
msgid "Array of `Identity` instances describing the subject of this certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:493
msgid "`Certificate#issuer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:495
msgid "The `Identity` of the Certificate's issuer (signer)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:497
msgid "`Certificate#subjectKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:499
msgid "The public key of the subject of the certificate, as a `Key` instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:501
msgid "`Certificate#issuerKey`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:503
msgid ""
"The public key of the signing issuer of this certificate, as a `Key` "
"instance. May be `undefined` if the issuer's key is unknown (e.g. on an "
"X509 certificate)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:506
msgid "`Certificate#serial`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:508
msgid ""
"The serial number of the certificate. As this is normally a 64-bit or "
"wider integer, it is returned as a Buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:511
msgid "`Certificate#purposes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:513
msgid ""
"Array of Strings indicating the X.509 key usage purposes that this "
"certificate is valid for. The possible strings at the moment are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:516
msgid "`'signature'` -- key can be used for digital signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:517
msgid ""
"`'identity'` -- key can be used to attest about the identity of the "
"signer                 (X.509 calls this `nonRepudiation`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:519
msgid "`'codeSigning'` -- key can be used to sign executable code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:520
msgid "`'keyEncryption'` -- key can be used to encrypt other keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:521
msgid "`'encryption'` -- key can be used to encrypt data (only applies for RSA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:522
msgid ""
"`'keyAgreement'` -- key can be used for key exchange protocols such as"
"                     Diffie-Hellman"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:524
msgid ""
"`'ca'` -- key can be used to sign other certificates (is a Certificate"
"           Authority)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:526
msgid "`'crl'` -- key can be used to sign Certificate Revocation Lists (CRLs)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:528
msgid "`Certificate#getExtension(nameOrOid)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:530
msgid ""
"Retrieves information about a certificate extension, if present, or "
"returns `undefined` if not. The string argument `nameOrOid` should be "
"either the OID (for X509 extensions) or the name (for OpenSSH extensions)"
" of the extension to retrieve."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:535
msgid "The object returned will have the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:537
msgid "`format` -- String, set to either `'x509'` or `'openssh'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:538
msgid "`name` or `oid` -- String, only one set based on value of `format`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:539
msgid "`data` -- Buffer, the raw data inside the extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:541
msgid "`Certificate#getExtensions()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:543
msgid ""
"Returns an Array of all present certificate extensions, in the same "
"manner and format as `getExtension()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:546
msgid "`Certificate#isExpired([when])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:548
msgid ""
"Tests whether the Certificate is currently expired (i.e. the `validFrom` "
"and `validUntil` dates specify a range of time that does not include the "
"current time)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:554
msgid ""
"`when` -- optional Date, if specified, tests whether the Certificate was "
"or           will be expired at the specified time instead of now"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:557 ../../source/sshpk_README.md:567
#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:579
msgid "Returns a Boolean."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:559
msgid "`Certificate#isSignedByKey(key)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:561
msgid ""
"Tests whether the Certificate was validly signed by the given (public) "
"Key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:565
msgid "`key` -- a Key instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:569
msgid "`Certificate#isSignedBy(certificate)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:571
msgid ""
"Tests whether this Certificate was validly signed by the subject of the "
"given certificate. Also tests that the issuer Identity of this "
"Certificate and the subject Identity of the other Certificate are "
"equivalent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:577
msgid "`certificate` -- another Certificate instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:581
msgid "`Certificate#fingerprint([hashAlgo])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:583
msgid ""
"Returns the X509-style fingerprint of the entire certificate (as a "
"Fingerprint instance). This matches what a web-browser or similar would "
"display as the certificate fingerprint and should not be confused with "
"the fingerprint of the subject's public key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:590
msgid "`hashAlgo` -- an optional String, any hash function name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:592
msgid "`Certificate#toBuffer([format])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:594
msgid "Serializes the Certificate to a Buffer and returns it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:598
msgid ""
"`format` -- an optional String, output format, one of `'openssh'`, "
"`'pem'` or             `'x509'`. Defaults to `'x509'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:601
msgid "Returns a Buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:603
msgid "`Certificate#toString([format])`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sshpk_README.md:605
msgid ""
"`format` -- an optional String, output format, one of `'openssh'`, "
"`'pem'` or             `'x509'`. Defaults to `'pem'`."
msgstr ""

